            body: 'A spreadsheet file remains fully editable by anyone who opens it, exactly right during active work, but not always desirable once the data is finalized and simply needs to be shared for viewing or printing. PDF, by contrast, presents data in a fixed, consistent, non-editable form that displays identically regardless of what device or software opens it, no risk of an accidental edit, no dependency on the recipient having Excel or a compatible spreadsheet app installed at all. This is exactly why converting to PDF makes sense specifically for the "share to view" case, print, archive, attach to an email or report, where the data\u2019s finished, fixed presentation matters more than continued editability.'
