            body: "Since the conversion process captures the video\u2019s actual real-time playback, which inherently includes its audio playing simultaneously alongside the visual content, the audio track gets captured and re-recorded together with the video in the same single pass, remaining correctly synchronized with the newly converted video output. This is exactly why audio doesn\u2019t require a separate extraction-and-recombination step, the unified real-time capture approach naturally keeps both tracks together and in sync throughout the entire conversion process."
