            heading: "Why an Array of Objects Is the Ideal Shape for This Conversion",
            body: "This conversion works most cleanly when the source JSON is an array of objects sharing a broadly similar structure, exactly the shape that maps naturally onto a table, each object becomes one table row, and the union of keys across all the objects becomes the table\u2019s column headers. This mirrors the same underlying logic used for converting JSON to CSV or Excel, all three are fundamentally translating the identical kind of list-of-similar-records data into whatever tabular format a specific destination, a spreadsheet, a CSV file, an HTML page, actually expects."
